  "title": "Class-II source, translated model, balanced coefficient jets, and obstruction boundary",
  "sector": "A",
  "statement": "For the hash-pinned A1 production coefficients and A10-A13 strict sharp cubes, all prior A13 reductions remain binding at T4. R-078 rewrites the R-076 third-order transport exactly as the bounded Hessian difference D^2M(U+tA)-D^2M(U) with explicit A^2 DA payload. At s=3/5 its input-maximum payment is X^(2/5)Y^(11/30), with Young slack 7/30 and moment 30/7. Subtracting every proved orientation from the complete endpoint and applying the causal projection once defines the canonical safe packet. For each component admitting a predictable-multiplier/current-increment factorisation, exact Doob algebra replaces the terminal coefficient by its future-control innovation; the corresponding unweighted coefficient coordinate has one Hilbert square-function bound. The declared high-U principal closes through the R-050 enhancement with moment 60/19. The exact full nonlinear packet-to-bracket decomposition, spatially weighted innovation bound, complete packet lower bound, controlled-shell one-use, and q=10/9 Nelson theorem remain open.",
  "scope": "PROVED-STRUCTURAL-TRANSLATION-UNIVERSAL-Q-BALANCED-JET-A7-RECONSTRUCTION-BACKWARD-HEAT-NPC-CONE-TIP-SAFE-HARVEST-ENDPOINT-LIFTED-CAUSAL-WICK-DOOB-ONE-FORM-LINEAR-PHASE-KERNEL-DIAGONAL-OFFDIAGONAL-TELESCOPE-RESONANT-PHASE-ORBIT-BESOV-INVARIANT-CURRENT-PRINCIPAL-TAYLOR-FIXED-CUTOFF-GRAPH-RECOVERY-SIGNED-TRANSPORT-BESOV-CAUSAL-PACKET-PAYLOAD-COMPARABLE-HESSIAN-DIFFERENCE-SAFE-PACKET-DOOB-BRACKET-AND-WEIGHTED-INNOVATION-BOUNDARY-REDUCTIONS-WITH-EXECUTED-NOGOS@FIXED-FLOOR-SHARP-CUBE on L=16 for the A1 production symbol and coefficients, three complex components in the six-real convention, rho_regularizer=1e-12, exact non-aliased Fourier products, common bounded entrywise-real-even scalar regulators, covariance-matched A7 Wick subtraction, and the A10-A13 dyadic rectangular-cube filtration. R-078 is exact at finite cutoff and cutoff-uniform for its analytic payload estimates at every fixed positive floor. It uses complete R-063/R-066 endpoint companions and smooth inhomogeneous Littlewood-Paley blocks only for analysis. Its Doob lemma applies to factorised bilinear components and is not an exact decomposition of the entire nonlinear safe packet. It does not prove that full decomposition, the spatially weighted future-control bound, the complete packet lower bound, extension to every finite-energy drift, controlled-shell one-use, Nelson, cutoff or floor removal, or any measure theorem.",
